    "project": "research/sidon_rho_counterfamily_audit_20261114/lean",
    "theorem": "SidonRhoCounterfamilyAudit.sidon_rho_counterfamily_certificate",
    "statement": "theorem sidon_rho_counterfamily_certificate : (∀ (p : ℕ) [NeZero p], 1902 < p → TwoStepCollisionAudit.DegreeTwoGeneric (increments p) ∧ (∀ h : ZMod p → Fin 20, p ≤ 951 * firstCollision p (transition p h) 0 ∧ firstCollision p (transition p h) 0 ≤ p) ∧ (p : ℝ) ≤ 951 * meanCollision p ∧ meanCollision p ≤ p ∧ meanCollision p = ∑ h, (uniformHashLaw p 20 (Nat.succ_pos 19) h).toReal * (firstCollision p (transition p h) 0 : ℝ) ∧ (∀ target : ZMod p, expectation (uniformWeights 20) (fun h => inDegree (increments p) h target) = 1 ∧ expectation (uniformWeights 20) (fun h => (inDegree (increments p) h target - 1)^2) = 19 / 20) ∧ (localLaw p).toOuterMeasure (GeneralTwoStepCollisionAudit.freshEvent (increments p) : Set (GeneralTwoStepCollisionAudit.JointSample (ZMod p) (Fin 20))) = ENNReal.ofReal ((7581 : ℝ) / (8000 * p))) ∧ (¬∃ C : ℝ, ∀ (p : ℕ) (hp : Nat.Prime p), 1902 < p → TwoStepCollisionAudit.DegreeTwoGeneric (increments p) → (@meanCollision p ⟨hp.ne_zero⟩)^2 ≤ C * p) ∧ Nat.Prime 10000019 ∧ (4 : ℝ) * 10000019 < (meanCollision 10000019)^2",
    "decl_sha256": "f4550e4315788edd2a98a3625997981779e48497f43bb1391580f556d5203953",
    "scope": "Explicit fixed20-step shifted Mian–Chowla finite-table rho counterfamily. Kernel checks the actual table Sidon property; for every p>1902 actual ZModp increments satisfy the unchanged literal degree0/1/2genericity predicate. Actual original20-label static hash walk embeds pointwise into bounded951 transition; no uniform distribution on Fin951 is assumed. Actual least firstcollision T satisfies p<=951T and T<=p for every hash. Actual uniform20-label product PMF has mean E with p<=951E and E<=p, in-degree variance19/20, and genuine fresh two-step event measure7581/(8000p). Nevertheless E²/p is unbounded over primes; direct negation of any real uniform square-root bound even retaining the literal local degree guard. Kernel checks prime10000019 and E²>4p. Strengthens prior known bounded fixed-support counterfamily by satisfying exact low-degree source conditions, credits Bernstein–Lange local dependency warning/OEIS finite table; no novelty or qualified random-increment-ensemble source refutation. No asymptotic random-table/practicalhash law, infinite greedy generation property, physicalhost/parser/hash/execution refinement. Only standard foundations/defaults, no holes/customaxioms/nativeproofevaluation/flags/limits/waivers/newcryptographicexperiment/spend/upload.",
